      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand you're feeling anxious and desire a quick solution, but it's crucial to use your best judgment in these situations. Not all fluctuations in blood sugar can be safely managed without professional guidance. An extra unit of rapid-acting insulin could significantly lower your blood glucose levels and potentially cause hypoglycemia (low blood sugar), which can be just as dangerous. It's best to avoid giving yourself additional insulin without supervision, as this could lead to complications. Please try to contact a healthcare professional as soon as reasonably possible, perhaps during their regular working hours, and if your condition worsens or your symptoms don't improve, consider seeking medical attention at an urgent care clinic or emergency room. Your health and safety are incredibly important.",
